WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.997
Named entity recognition is a token-classification task.

00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:10.602
We want to identify spans such as person names, organizations, and locations inside a sentence.

00:00:10.602 --> 00:00:16.322
The pipeline API makes the workflow simple: create an NER pipeline, pass in the text,

00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:20.322
and inspect each returned entity, group, and confidence score.

00:00:20.322 --> 00:00:26.622
The grouping option combines subword predictions back into readable entity spans.

00:00:26.622 --> 00:00:32.642
Depending on the Transformers version, you may see aggregation_strategy used instead of the older

00:00:32.642 --> 00:00:35.867
grouped_entities argument.

00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:41.437
Run the example with a different sentence and watch how the model handles multi-word names.

00:00:41.437 --> 00:00:47.932
Also remember that a generic NER checkpoint is trained on a particular label set and domain.

00:00:47.932 --> 00:00:51.997
If your application needs clinical entities, legal entities, or custom categories,

00:00:51.997 --> 00:00:59.902
choose a domain-appropriate checkpoint or fine-tune a model on labeled examples for your own entity types.
